<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding the conditional probability of two events, their complements and union</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A\) and \(B\) are two events such that \(P(A)={@p_a@}\), \(P(B)={@p_b@}\) and \(P(A\cap B)={@p_anb@}\).</p>
<p>Find the probability of the following events below, and give your answers in two decimal places.</p>
<p>a. \(P(A \cup B) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>b. \( P(B|A) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>c. \(P((A|B)^C)= \)[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p>d. \(P(A|B^C) = \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked solution</b></p>
<p>a. Find \(P(A \cup B)\)</p> 
<p>We have: \( P(A \cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A \cap B)\)</p>
<p>Then \( P(A \cup B)={@p_a@}+{@p_b@}-{@p_anb@}\)</p>
<p>Therefore, \( P(A \cup B)={@ta1@}\)</p>
<hr>
<p>b. Find  \( P(B|A)\)</p>
<p>We have:</p>
<p>\( P(B|A)=\frac{P(B \cap A)}{P(A)} \) </p>
<p>\( P(B|A)= \frac{{@p_anb@}}{{@p_a@}} \)</p>
<p>Therefore \(P(B|A)={@ta2@}\)</p>
<hr>
<p>c. Find \( P(A|B)^C\)
</p><p>We have: \( P((A|B)^C)=1-P(A|B) \), and \(P(A|B)= \frac{P(A \cap B)}{P(B)} \)</p>
<p>So \( P((A|B)^C)=1-\frac{P(A \cap B)}{P(B)}\). Then</p><p>
</p><p>\( P((A|B)^C)=1-\frac{@p_anb@}{@p_b@} \)</p>
<p>\( P((A|B)^C)={@ta3@} \)</p>
<hr>
<p>d. Find \( P(A|B^C)\) </p>
<p>\( P(A|B^C)=\frac{P(A \cap B^C)}{P(B^C)}=\frac{P(A)-P(A \cap B)}{1-P(B)}\)</p>
<p>Then \( P(A|B^C)=\frac{{@p_a@}-{@p_anb@}}{{@1@}-{@p_b@}}\)</p><p> Therefore \( P(A|B^C) ={@ta4@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
